# FABLE-SONNET-UNIT-LEVEL-ROOTS-20260923-117 generalized the own-array
# helpers past the two literal roots "for"/"node". FABLE-SONNET-ARRAY-
# WRITE-DISPATCH-20260923-119 found and fixed a write-dispatch ordering
# gap for that generalization, then fable corrected the generalization's
# MEANING for any OTHER root: root\name[idx] denotes a field OF root's
# type, never a same-named sibling own array. FABLE-SONNET-NODE-ROOT-
# 20260923-121 (author Q9) then removed node/for's own single-hop
# own-table lookup entirely -- node\name[idx]/for\name[idx] are no longer
# a spelling gate onto the own table either; see
# unit_array_write_general_root_no_field.lm2 for the resulting uniform
# "unsupported index" refusal (node/for included). This fixture is left
# covering only what a bare own name has always meant: the own-table
# gate/lookup itself, with no root at all.
fn: build () int
    []: int buf 3
    buf[0]: 6
    if: buf[0] != 6
        return: 97
    if: length(buf) != 3
        return: 96
    return: 0

return: build()
